AU  - Gounot, G
TI  - Blood profile of a dairy herd with exceptionally high mortality
T2  - POINT VETERINAIRE
AB  - Problems in a herd of 60 dairy cows with a history of sporadic lameness and high mortality in adult cows were assessed, with the agreement of the farmer, by wide-ranging blood biochemistry and haematology investigations on eight cows selected at random. The haematology screening was extended to the whole herd in order to research the abnormalities found. There was a predominate lymphopenia. Monocytosis, neutrophilia and eosinophilia were also widely seen. It appeared that Babesia divergens was present in the herd without producing clinical signs. However, Anaplasma phagocytophilum, which was highly suspected empirically, was finally evidenced and also Lyme disease. A general but short duration tetracycline treatment provided temporary improvement. It was difficult to establish the status of fasciolosis in this herd.
