AB  - To the Editor: Vitiligo is a depigmenting skin disorder that can have a substantial effect on patients' quality of life. In their report on two phase 3 trials of ruxolitinib cream (Topical Ruxolitinib Evaluation in Vitiligo Study 1 and 2), Rosmarin et al. (Oct. 20 issue)(1) found that ruxolitinib cream was effective for repigmentation of the skin in patients with vitiligo. The adverse events of ruxolitinib cream appeared to be limited, but the follow-up was restricted to 1 year. In patients who were treated with ruxolitinib for polycythemia vera and myelofibrosis, systemic exposure to oral ruxolitinib was associated with an . . .
