TI  - ECONOMIC-LOSSES DUE TO DISEASES AND CONSTRAINTS FOR DAIRY DEVELOPMENT IN KANGRA DISTRICT OF HIMACHAL-PRADESH
T2  - INDIAN JOURNAL OF ANIMAL SCIENCES
AB  - The study was carried out during 1990-91 mainly to examine the economic losses and constraints for dairy development following a multi-stage random-sampling technique. The analysis of data collected from 100 dairy farmers (61 small, 25 medium and 14 large) through personal interview method revealed that percentage of mortality increased due to increase in dairy herd size because of close contact of animals; in respect of morbidity no specific relationship was realised. The economic losses due to mortality and morbidity were higher on small and large farms respectively. These could be due to poor financial position of small farmers and easy access of large farmers to veterinary facilities. High cost of fodder and concentrates, scarcity of fodder, poor quality of agricultural land, illiteracy, scattered and fragmented holdings, lack of grazing lands and infestation of weeds and obnoxious grasses were reported to be the major problems for dairy development. The government must strengthen, extend, intensify the dairy development programme particularly with public involvement so that the equality between demand for and supply of mi Ik and milk products can be attained.
